{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0033", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e8d2b074901a8e4fa84aa2cbaaec0dee0ccfd9453788a70f5f403e7487115711", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we define exact functors.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:53c4e0a9aa1f74a8ef06d6a8ab0c9f4dfca3e50d37048d53707518d4141a517b", "unit_id": "tag:0033:paragraph-0001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0033", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$F$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-exact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:34b7570da4cb232e330153246df7a292f5011752eb13831d106b48a19b3e254e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:78b8c7d33b56259cc9d2288285808581fbd603ccc738dd427d4ca6486949c8e6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a functor.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Suppose all finite limits exist in <MATH_0002>.\nWe say <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>left exact<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if it commutes\nwith all finite limits.\n<STRUCT_0003> Suppose all finite colimits exist in <MATH_0004>.\nWe say <MATH_0005> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>right exact<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if it commutes\nwith all finite colimits.\n<STRUCT_0004> We say <MATH_0006> is <TEXTITOPEN_0003>exact<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if it is both left and right\nexact.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6bcd4a7563147e54c7bcdbb2e1692de0138b1fb9f03df5827173092e3b9e6fff", "unit_id": "tag:0034:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0033", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$F$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-finite-limits-exist}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-left-exact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4d49231b288129d4403abd2fc02e042fc7a047fbe5e97015f1b119f17929d028", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5dca79faba10b9539fe9ee0a45080011d2dee47190590bd1985979754074dcff", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a functor.\nSuppose all finite limits exist in <MATH_0002>,\nsee Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is left exact,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0004> commutes with finite products and equalizers, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0005> transforms a final object of <MATH_0006>\ninto a final object of <MATH_0007>, and commutes with fibre products.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2e4b58495d05299d9081d5a993eba6957482c304488fc77ee698536b2433ca6c", "unit_id": "tag:0035:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0033", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$a, b : A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$a, b$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n(A \\times_{a, B, b} A)\\times_{(\\text{pr}_1, \\text{pr}_2), A \\times A, \\Delta} A.\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-limits-products-equalizers}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a62f1c52b8fa09131971e5b544483e23ea22f9e8bc26d6b92f77e1562fa23933", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:138c8121be63743a297728c1c6124db5dba009df5e95d9ccf240189fe93eba22", "source_text": "Lemma <REF_0001> shows that (2) implies (1).\nSuppose (3) holds. The fibre product over the final object is the product.\nIf <MATH_0001> are morphisms of <MATH_0002>, then the\nequalizer of <MATH_0003> is\n<MATH_0004>\nThus (3) implies (2). Finally (1) implies (3) because\nthe empty limit is a final object, and fibre products are limits.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fb18a50b4047e0bd72aa2a6acc1091dfd6f455464934c42ffa2d47f93268a2ad", "unit_id": "tag:0035:proof"}
